<title>UK: LGardner pretax surges, to raise 5.6 mln stg.</title>
<headline>LGardner pretax surges, to raise 5.6 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		15.6		   vs 12.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 4.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 6.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Pretax		     2.5		    vs 1.8</p>
<p> Turnover		   22.0		   vs 16.5</p>
<p>NOTE - Newly-floated UK engineering firm L Gardner Group Plc said it planned a placing and open offer of 3.2 million shares at 175p to raise 5.3 million stg net of expenses. The group wants to buy precision parts firm Sloman Engineering for 1.7 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 2.72		   vs 1.94</p>
<p> Interest payable	 0.19		   vs 0.16</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.85		   vs 0.62</p>
<p> Net taxed		  1.68		   vs 1.52</p>
<p> Retained profit	  1.01		   vs 0.65</p>
<p> Pay date		   n/a</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 25</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Nov 7</p>
<p>NOTE - The group, releasing its maiden results since flotation last November, said its open offer was on a two-for-7 basis. It said the first two months had started well, noting it would review acquisitions and saw propects for organic growth.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
